Error [E0702]: An FFI boundary rejects call `bad` uses capability `&` outside `#Unsafe`
  --> tests/ui/ffi_bad_type.jet:8:11
    |
  8 |     print(bad(&value))
    |           ^^^
 Why: A foreign capability can write to or transfer ownership of Jet storage, so a raw call needs an audited boundary
 Fix: Call `bad` inside `#Unsafe("…") { … }`, or expose it through a generated typed binding
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0702
